        # The 120-char base-length guard below leaves headroom.
        # Pre-bumped from 16 bytes — was overflow-prone for any base
        # name >11 chars (e.g. `f64v2_add_ptr` direct call constructed
        # `f64v2_add_ptr_ptr` = 18 bytes; the overflow corrupted
        # adjacent stack data and returned wrong values from any fn
        # call that hit this dispatch path).
